# M6 flow (D-017, D-047): game over in Bad Ischl -> continue restarts Bad
# Ischl, not the run's first stage (Strobl). Title flow with the run
# started in Strobl: flow_m6_strobl_to_bad_ischl's inputs to the start of
# Bad Ischl play (2942: score 17300, 3 lives, 34 Oblaten). Then three
# tries of the first 150 frames of bad_ischl_solver.replay (the
# route's first jumps, back down onto the street at col 26) and standing:
# Kurgast #1 walks into her (deaths at 3322, 3912, 4502, each try 590
# frames: 60 dying + 150 intro + 380 of play); game over at 4562; START
# at 4642 -> the Bad Ischl intro (4643) and play at its start (4793): 3
# lives, score 0, 0 Oblaten, Normal. D-102 (E42): Strobl's time_limit 230
# (was 240) shortens its tally by 10 frames, so everything comes 10 frames
# earlier (10 idle frames fewer before Bad Ischl play).
level  = strobl
